{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An upgraded terminal run with an open pull request is permanently excluded from reconciliation, so a pre-existing in-progress label can remain and block a later approved run."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"unusual","reason":"After a posting identity change and a lost retry response, recovery can publish a duplicate lifecycle comment."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A valid re-approval within the same timestamp second can be rejected indefinitely until an owner approves again."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A run linking many inaccessible issues can exhaust every poll's request budget before a later accessible issue receives lifecycle updates."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A resumed label plan can retain a restored in-progress label alongside needs-you, causing the issue to remain ineligible for the queue."}]}